<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §5 — the deep-drill response event.

    ⛔ BAN 6, ABSOLUTE, and this def is where it bites hardest: "no text —
    letter, def description, commentary line, art note — ever describes the
    response beyond 'massive mechanoid movement'." The label and letter below
    say what a Jawa at a drill head can SEE and HEAR, from where they are
    standing, and stop. They do not say what is coming, why, what it wants,
    what it will do, whether it can be fought, or whether it will leave. The
    player experience the spec asks for is "dig deep enough and very bad
    things happen. No one's quite sure what." — so nobody, including this file,
    is allowed to be sure.

    No <description> field at all: an IncidentDef description is player-visible
    in the debug/incident menus, and every honest sentence that could go there
    would breach ban 6.

    FIRING: no storyteller entry of our own. category DeepDrillInfestation puts
    this def in the pool vanilla's already-present
    StorytellerComp_DeepDrillInfestation rolls (MTB 20 days per usable drill,
    difficulty-scaled, on the storyteller base def). See the worker file for
    why the spec's INVENTED "MTB 6 days per tapped drill" is NOT taken: a
    second comp would raise ORDINARY infestation rates on every non-Cathedral
    map in the game, and that is too high a price for one number.

    targetTags mirror vanilla DeepDrillInfestation's exactly — the storyteller
    comp filters on its own allowedTargetTags list, so a narrower set here
    would just make the incident unreachable on some map types.

    pointsScaleable true: the worker multiplies parms.points by 2-3x, which
    only means anything if the storyteller has scaled them first.
  -->

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_DeepDrillCathedralResponse</defName>
    <label>deep signal</label>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.RustCathedralHum.RUT_IncidentWorker_CathedralResponse</workerClass>
    <category>DeepDrillInfestation</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
      <li>Map_TempIncident</li>
      <li>Map_Misc</li>
      <li>Map_RaidBeacon</li>
    </targetTags>
    <letterLabel>Deep signal</letterLabel>
    <letterText>The drill head went quiet, and then everything did. The hum is gone.\n\nOut past the wall line, something very large is moving, and it is moving this way.</letterText>
    <letterDef>ThreatBig</letterDef>
    <baseChance>1</baseChance>
    <pointsScaleable>true</pointsScaleable>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
